<description>
Paint each pink control pixel as a teal horizontal bar whose reach equals the foreground counts on that row.

Input structure
- The grid has a dominant background color and one or more pink control pixels.
- Each marker row has exactly one pink pixel; all other non-background pixels
  in that row are counters.
Rule
- Start from an all-background output grid.
- For each pink pixel, count non-background pixels strictly to its left and
  strictly to its right in the same row.
- Paint teal from c - left_count through c + right_count on that row.
Key insight
- The foreground pixels are not copied; only their counts on each side of
  each pink marker encode the teal bar length.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "pink control pixels on rows with other non-background counter pixels",
  "transform": "erase all input foreground; for each pink pixel, count non-background pixels strictly left and right on its row and paint a teal horizontal segment extending that many cells from the pink pixel"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 10x10, bg=7 [observed]
  markers:
    count: 4-5 pink (color 6) pixels, each on a distinct row
    placement: exactly 1 pink pixel per marker row; remaining rows are distractor-only
    per_marker_row: |
      left_count (non-bg pixels strictly left of pink): 0-5
      right_count (non-bg pixels strictly right of pink): 0-5
      bar_length = left_count + right_count + 1: 3-7
      constraint: bar must fit in grid (col - left_count >= 0, col + right_count < W)
      counter pixels are scattered (not necessarily adjacent to pink)
      counter colors: any except pink and bg; may repeat; teal (8) is allowed
  distractor_rows:
    rows without pink: 5-6 rows
    non-bg pixels per distractor row: 0-7; colors arbitrary (no pink)
  output:
    grid same size, filled with bg
    each marker row gets a contiguous teal (8) bar from col-left_count to col+right_count
    all other rows remain bg

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid 10x10 with bg=7.
    2. Pick 4-5 distinct marker rows. For each, sample pink column and left/right counts
       such that bar_length in [3,7] and bar fits within [0, W-1].
    3. Build output: place teal bar on each marker row.
    4. Build input from output by inverting:
       a. For each marker row, place pink pixel at its column.
       b. Scatter left_count non-bg pixels at random positions strictly left of pink,
          and right_count strictly right, using random non-pink non-bg colors.
       c. Fill remaining marker-row cells with bg.
    5. For each non-marker row, scatter 0-7 distractor pixels at random columns
       using random non-pink non-bg colors.
```
